' Your task (Chapter 3, Question 2): draw the UML class diagram for the
' Vehicle / Car / ElectricCar / Chargeable code.
'
' Define each type as a box, then connect them with the right arrows. One box
' (Chargeable) is filled in as an example — complete the other three and add the
' relationships.
'
' PlantUML cheat-sheet:
'   interface Name { + method() : Type }
'   abstract class Name { # field : Type }
'   class Name { - field : Type }
'   Parent    <|-- Child    ' generalization: Child extends Parent
'   Interface <|.. Class    ' realization:    Class implements Interface
' (Putting the parent/interface on the LEFT of the arrow keeps it on top.)

interface Chargeable {
  + charge() : void
}

abstract class Vehicle {
#make : String
+Vehicle(make:String)
+maxSpeed():int {abstract}
}

class Car extends Vehicle {
#make : String
+Car(make:String)
+maxSpeed():int
}

class ElectricCar extends Vehicle implements charge {
- batteryLevel : int
# make : string
+ElectricCar(make:String)
+maxSpeed():int
+charge():void
}

